1
00:00:01,410 --> 00:00:04,230
Hi. I'm Malcolm Stewart.

2
00:00:04,230 --> 00:00:05,580
John Marchetta.

3
00:00:05,580 --> 00:00:09,200
Sit down, sit down.

4
00:00:09,200 --> 00:00:11,960
Susan has told me a great deal about you.

5
00:00:11,960 --> 00:00:13,790
She says you're quite a man.

6
00:00:13,790 --> 00:00:14,310
She says

7
00:00:14,310 --> 00:00:17,970
a lot of wonderful things about you too, Mr. Stewart.

8
00:00:17,970 --> 00:00:20,450
That's always nice to hear, Mr. Marchetta.

9
00:00:20,450 --> 00:00:21,490
Call me John.

10
00:00:21,490 --> 00:00:24,050
May I call you Malcolm?

11
00:00:24,050 --> 00:00:25,920
Let's talk business.

12
00:00:25,920 --> 00:00:27,910
That's music to my ears.

13
00:00:27,910 --> 00:00:28,620
I understand

14
00:00:28,620 --> 00:00:30,860
you used to be in the construction business.

15
00:00:30,860 --> 00:00:33,930
Yup. Forty-three years.

16
00:00:33,930 --> 00:00:35,680
Here's a brief description

17
00:00:35,680 --> 00:00:42,110
of forty-three years of on-the-job training.

18
00:00:42,110 --> 00:00:44,840
That is some history!

19
00:00:44,840 --> 00:00:46,830
You're a valuable asset, Malcolm.

20
00:00:46,830 --> 00:00:48,660
Very valuable.

21
00:00:48,660 --> 00:00:50,810
Thank you.

22
00:00:50,810 --> 00:00:54,610
Yup. Forty-three years.

23
00:00:54,610 --> 00:00:57,080
Half that time in my own construction company.

24
00:00:57,080 --> 00:01:00,880
Big jobs--factories, shopping malls.

25
00:01:00,880 --> 00:01:02,740
That kind of thing.

26
00:01:02,740 --> 00:01:04,200
Then you retired.

27
00:01:04,200 --> 00:01:05,860
Yes.

28
00:01:05,860 --> 00:01:07,830
After my wife died,

29
00:01:07,830 --> 00:01:09,740
and I felt I should spend more time

30
00:01:09,740 --> 00:01:12,890
with my children and grandchildren.

31
00:01:12,890 --> 00:01:14,390
I lived in Florida,

32
00:01:14,390 --> 00:01:15,990
and they lived in New York.

33
00:01:15,990 --> 00:01:16,800
I understand.

34
00:01:16,800 --> 00:01:19,140
My dautghter Cami lives in New York.

35
00:01:19,140 --> 00:01:21,910
I like being near her.

36
00:01:21,910 --> 00:01:22,940
When I came here,

37
00:01:22,940 --> 00:01:25,990
I planned to take a few months off.

38
00:01:25,990 --> 00:01:30,310
Relax with the family and then look for some work.

39
00:01:30,310 --> 00:01:33,120
Put my experience on the line ...

40
00:01:33,120 --> 00:01:34,530
but, unfortunately,

41
00:01:34,530 --> 00:01:37,800
there isn't any work for a retired person my age.

42
00:01:37,800 --> 00:01:38,560
Sometimes there is,

43
00:01:38,560 --> 00:01:40,820
and sometimes there isn't.

44
00:01:40,820 --> 00:01:42,900
Well, I'm involved with an organization,

45
00:01:42,900 --> 00:01:46,320
and we're trying to resolve that problem.

46
00:01:46,320 --> 00:01:47,660
What's that?

47
00:01:47,660 --> 00:01:49,080
TOPS.

48
00:01:49,080 --> 00:01:55,230
T-O-P-S--means Talented Older People's Society.

49
00:01:55,230 --> 00:01:57,120
I'd like to be a member.

50
00:01:57,120 --> 00:01:58,350
How much are the dues?

51
00:01:58,350 --> 00:02:00,990
There are no dues.

52
00:02:00,990 --> 00:02:04,340
The organization serves major companies in this city.

53
00:02:04,340 --> 00:02:05,870
Why?

54
00:02:05,870 --> 00:02:08,240
Because our members are men and women like you.

55
00:02:08,240 --> 00:02:12,390
Experienced, talented, retired.

56
00:02:12,390 --> 00:02:14,330
But our members want to go out there

57
00:02:14,330 --> 00:02:15,730
and use their talents.

58
00:02:15,730 --> 00:02:18,290
They want to work.

59
00:02:18,290 --> 00:02:20,370
That is fantastic, John!

60
00:02:20,370 --> 00:02:24,290
I've got an idea for you, Malcolm.

61
00:02:24,290 --> 00:02:25,770
Just fill out this form for me.

62
00:02:25,770 --> 00:02:27,380
It'll only take a few minutes.

63
00:02:27,380 --> 00:02:28,360
Sit right here,

64
00:02:28,360 --> 00:02:30,370
and do it while I talk to my secretary.

65
00:02:30,370 --> 00:02:33,970
When I get back, we'll talk about my new factory.

66
00:02:33,970 --> 00:02:35,610
My company is a member of TOPS.

67
00:02:35,610 --> 00:02:39,390
So I try hard to find opportunities for people like you.

68
00:02:39,390 --> 00:02:40,730
Malcolm.

69
00:02:40,730 --> 00:02:42,100
And when I see an opportunity,

70
00:02:42,100 --> 00:02:44,130
I can act on it.

71
00:02:44,130 --> 00:02:50,210
Well, I can use your brainpower on the job right now.

72
00:02:50,210 --> 00:02:51,260
Have you got time this morning

73
00:02:51,260 --> 00:02:53,820
to go over to the construction site with me?

74
00:02:53,820 --> 00:02:55,760
I'd like to have you meet my foreman--

75
00:02:55,760 --> 00:02:57,760
get some background on the job.

76
00:02:57,760 --> 00:03:00,010
I've got plenty of time.

77
00:03:00,010 --> 00:03:01,510
I'll be right back.

78
00:03:01,510 --> 00:03:21,190
We'll go over to the job site together.

79
00:03:21,190 --> 00:03:25,490
Malcolm, you worked on the Spaceport project?

80
00:03:25,490 --> 00:03:28,640
My company was the contractor.

81
00:03:28,640 --> 00:03:30,880
I built the theater there

82
00:03:30,880 --> 00:03:32,710
with my own two hands, practically.

83
00:03:32,710 --> 00:03:33,610
I understand.

84
00:03:33,610 --> 00:03:33,980
Well,

85
00:03:33,980 --> 00:03:37,040
I'm glad to see you two guys getting along so well

86
00:03:37,040 --> 00:03:38,400
because, Danny,

87
00:03:38,400 --> 00:03:39,530
Malcolm is on the TOPS team.

88
00:03:39,530 --> 00:03:42,060
He's going to be working with you for a while.

89
00:03:42,060 --> 00:03:45,030
His experience will be valuable to both of us.

90
00:03:45,030 --> 00:03:46,780
Welcome aboard, Malcolm!

91
00:03:46,780 --> 00:03:48,220
I'm going back to my office.

92
00:03:48,220 --> 00:03:49,640
Give me a call later, Malcolm.

93
00:03:49,640 --> 00:03:52,710
I'll tell you the time and date of the next TOPS meeting.

94
00:03:52,710 --> 00:03:53,920
I'd like you to meet the group.

95
00:03:53,920 --> 00:03:55,100
I will, John.

96
00:03:55,100 --> 00:03:56,870
And again--thanks.

97
00:03:56,870 --> 00:03:59,150
No ... thank you.

98
00:03:59,150 --> 00:04:03,300
And thank Susan.

99
00:04:03,300 --> 00:04:04,940
He's quite a man.

100
00:04:04,940 --> 00:04:08,290
A real inspiration for me.

101
00:04:08,290 --> 00:04:10,450
[04:07.02]OK, Danny.

102
00:04:10,450 --> 00:04:10,970
I know you didn't expect to have me around,

103
00:04:10,970 --> 00:04:13,580
but I think I can be of some help to you.

104
00:04:13,580 --> 00:04:15,000
Let me tell you something, Malcolm.

105
00:04:15,000 --> 00:04:16,200
With your background and experience,

106
00:04:16,200 --> 00:04:17,450
I can learn something

107
00:04:17,450 --> 00:04:19,650
... and I do need some advice on a difficult problem.

108
00:04:19,650 --> 00:04:24,650
Let me show you this.

109
00:04:24,650 --> 00:04:28,360
I don't want to give you a final opinion

110
00:04:28,360 --> 00:04:32,010
without studying these building plans more carefully.

111
00:04:32,010 --> 00:04:35,650
But a simple solution might be

112
00:04:35,650 --> 00:04:37,500
to move the air-conditioning units

113
00:04:37,500 --> 00:04:40,500
instead of redesigning the entire system.

114
00:04:40,500 --> 00:04:44,780
It might be simpler and less expensive .

115
00:04:44,780 --> 00:04:47,860
You just earned your weight in gold, Malcolm.

116
00:04:47,860 --> 00:04:52,760
Welcome aboard!

117
00:04:52,760 --> 00:04:54,790
It all happened so quickly!

118
00:04:54,790 --> 00:04:56,530
I can't believe it!

119
00:04:56,530 --> 00:04:58,940
I'm glad Mr. Marchetta was so helpful.

120
00:04:58,940 --> 00:05:00,360
He was more than helpful.

121
00:05:00,360 --> 00:05:03,700
He actually took me to meet his foreman.

122
00:05:03,700 --> 00:05:06,320
I'm thrilled for you, Grandpa.

123
00:05:06,320 --> 00:05:09,420
I don't know how to thank you, Susan.

124
00:05:09,420 --> 00:05:11,740
You're a wonderful granddaughter.

125
00:05:11,740 --> 00:05:13,760
It's good to see you so happy.

126
00:05:13,760 --> 00:05:16,320
I'll be at the construction site tomorrow.

127
00:05:16,320 --> 00:05:17,850
What are you doing tomorrow night?

128
00:05:17,850 --> 00:05:18,800
I'm not doing anything.

129
00:05:18,800 --> 00:05:20,240
Why?

130
00:05:20,240 --> 00:05:22,180
How about a date with your grandfather?

131
00:05:22,180 --> 00:05:25,170
I owe you a good steak dinner.

132
00:05:25,170 --> 00:05:26,800
I'll accept.

133
00:05:26,800 --> 00:05:27,730
Tomorrow night.

134
00:05:27,730 --> 00:05:29,500
You and me. Dinner.

135
00:05:29,500 --> 00:05:31,070
What time?

136
00:05:31,070 --> 00:05:32,960
I'll pick you up here at seven .

137
00:05:32,960 --> 00:05:34,260
Is that OK?

138
00:05:34,260 --> 00:05:35,460
I can't wait!

139
00:05:35,460 --> 00:05:36,310
And you can tell me

140
00:05:36,310 --> 00:05:39,320
all about your first full day back on the job.

141
00:05:39,320 --> 00:05:42,320
It's a deal!
